# Line-ending policy.
#
# Host-side shell scripts must stay LF: a clone on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise give them CRLF, and bash rejects the
# shebang line. Inputs must stay LF because the engine's awk parser treats a
# trailing \r as part of the field value (a 15-residue sequence then fails with
# "ERROR 2 : invalid residue at 16").
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.inp   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.cff   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# The engine is kept exactly as delivered by its author, CRLF and all. The
# container runs dos2unix over it at build time, so the line endings here are
# provenance, not a functional requirement — do not let git renormalise them.
engine/** -text
